trigger:
Hey there!
{break}
My name is Taye, and I heard from our mutual friend Jackie that you're the person with the know-how to make flares that can clear Muck. I'm working on an exploration project that involves some caves, but they're covered in Muck, and it's making it tough to navigate.
{break}
I have a **Thermoblaster** that can help with the creation of the flares, and I think your skills would be super helpful for our mission. Would you be interested in joining me on this venture and putting your skills to the test?
{break}
We'll need some lumber for the flares, and Watt's supplies are running low. Can you bring some with you? **40 lumber** should be more than enough for now.
{break}
Looking forward to hearing back from you, and let's uncover the secrets of those caves together!
{break}
- Taye

The name is **Jackie**. I'm glad we found ya before the Muckers did.{break}
Who are the Muckers?{break}
That's a question we're still trying to answer... {break}
One day, the news is reporting some plants are mysteriously dying...{break}
...the next day we're here, in The Grove, fighting to rebuild the world we lost.{break}
See all these people around? These are the survivors. This is **The Collective**. {break}
Most of them ended up here the same way you did. {break}
I take it you don't remember much before I picked ya up? {break}
I'll spare you all the details... {break}
My main concern right now is making sure you're okay. {break}
I'm going to go collect a few important items that will help get you back on your feet. {break}
In the meantime, head out that front gate and meet with **Billy**, The Collective's head of construction. {break}
Billy can get you some new clothes and tell you a little bit more about this new world we're living in.

I hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to you today as a collector of rare fish who is in search of some unique specimens. I have heard of your reputation as a skilled fisherman and was hoping that you might be able to assist me in my search.
{break}
Specifically, I am in search of fish of rare colors that I have not been able to find in my local area. After conducting extensive research, I believe that these fish can only be found in the depths of caves that are not easily accessible. Given your expertise in fishing and your knowledge of the local area, I believe that you may be able to help me locate these elusive specimens.
{break}
I understand that this may be a difficult and dangerous task, and I am willing to compensate you for your time and effort accordingly. Additionally, I would be interested in visiting you to discuss the specifics of what I am looking for and to see your own collection of rare fish.
{break}
Please let me know if you are available and willing to assist me in my search. I look forward to hearing back from you soon.
{break}
Sincerely,{break}
Matt Hue

Ah, the Zzyzyxy! This is a fascinating fish, and its name has an interesting backstory as well. You see, the name "Zzyzyxy" dates back to the "before times," when language was still evolving, and people were experimenting with new words and concepts.{break}The word "Zzyzyxy" was created as a challenge to linguists to come up with a word that began and ended with the letter "Z." It quickly caught on and became a popular word among linguists and language enthusiasts.
{break}
Interestingly enough, the Zzyzyxy fish was named after this word because of its unique coloration and pattern, which reminded early explorers of the exotic and unusual nature of the word "Zzyzyxy."
{break}
I'm thrilled to have this fish in my collection, and I'm sure it will continue to be a source of fascination and wonder for many years to come. If you don't mind, I'll be taking all of them, for display.

Congratulations on finishing your home, {username}! 🎉
{break}
Here's a quick housewarming gift. Others can leave you packages if you place this near your robot!
{break}
Tell you what, if you find someone you don't know, and like their home, let me know and I'll leave a gift in their mailbox!

Dear {playerName},
{break}
I heard that you have a new experimental **Thermolite**, which can process stone. I would like to commission you to create Basalt Bricks using your device. Basalt is highly durable and resistant to wear and tear, and these bricks would be in high demand for construction projects in Watt.
{break}
If you are interested, please let me know, and we can discuss the details and compensation.
{break}
Thank you for considering this opportunity.
{break}
Best regards,
{break}
Tann Sonn

Did you manage to bring the basalt material for the bricks?
{break}
No, I'm sorry if I wasn't clear in my letter. I need you to create some Basalt Bricks for me using your Thermolite.
{break}
You mean you don't know how to create basalt bricks, or even where to find basalt?
{break}
...
{break}
Very well then.
{break}
Basalt is a volcanic rock, but in this area, it can be found in caves or by digging down. Bring me 100 basalt and I can show you how to create bricks from them.

Hey {playerName}, welcome back. I see you brought the raw basalt. Excellent.
{break}
Let's get started. First, we need to load the basalt into the Thermolite.
{break}
Oh that's right, you don't have your Thermolite here with you.
{break}
You can use the one here in Watt, but be wary -- you'll pay a fee for using it, rather than the one next to your own robot.
{break}
Basalt is a bit harder to smooth out, but we're not making smooth basalt, and you can just melt the stone into a rough shape. Here, take this mold, and make as many basalt bricks as you can with it.

Wow, these are some really impressive basalt bricks, {playerName}. You did a great job. Thank you so much!
{break}
This will be a big help for my construction projects. I was really struggling to find enough basalt bricks to finish the job, but now I have plenty to work with.

Dear {playerName},
{break}
My name is Mabel and I work at Brickleberry Farms. I have heard about your amazing talent for growing plants and I wanted to reach out to you about a discovery I have made.
{break}
Recently, I came across a new type of plant that I believe has incredible potential for growth and cultivation. However, my fellow townspeople have ridiculed me for suggesting that we try to grow this plant in a cave. I understand their skepticism, but I truly believe that this plant has the potential to revolutionize agriculture.
{break}
That's why I'm writing to you. I have heard that you are a skilled and knowledgeable plant grower, and I am hoping that you might be willing to try growing this new plant in your own space. I can send you seeds and provide you with any information I have about the plant.
{break}
I understand that this is a risky venture, but I truly believe that this plant has the potential to be something incredible. If you're willing to take a chance and help me prove the skeptics wrong, I would be forever grateful.
{break}
Thank you for considering my request, and I hope to hear from you soon.
{break}
Sincerely,
{break}
Mabel

Thank you so much for coming to visit me at Brickleberry Farms. {break} I'm sorry that the original plant I showed you died in the sunlight - I had no idea that it was so sensitive to light. {break} However, I still have hope for this new type of plant that I want to share with you.
{break}
I've managed to save some seeds from the original plant, and I've been keeping them in a **dark, cool place**. {break} These seeds only grow in the dark, and I think they might have the potential to thrive in a cave or other dark environment.
{break}
If you're willing to give it a try, I would be thrilled if you would plant these seeds and see if you can get them to grow. {break} I don't have a lot of information about the plant, but I can tell you that it's a hardy variety that is resistant to pests and diseases.

I am absolutely thrilled to tell you that the seeds you planted have grown into beautiful and healthy plants! And even more exciting, I discovered that they have a hidden property - they repel muckers!
{break}
This is incredible news for us at Brickleberry Farms. Muckers have always been a huge problem for our crops, and we've struggled to find effective ways to keep them away. But with these new plants, we might finally have a solution!

 Oh, you're here to learn about my quick growing plants? I see. Well, I have a secret method for growing them that I've perfected over the years.
{break}
Roberto: Shroomer Sam told you about my secret, did he? That guy is always spreading rumors. But it's true that my plants are the envy of the county.

Hmm, wheat seeds, you say? That's an interesting offer. I do have a weakness for those. Alright, I'll make a deal with you. Give me those wheat seeds, and I'll tell you my secret method for growing quick plants.
{break}
It's all about the fertilizer mix, you see. I've been experimenting with different combinations for years, and I've finally found the perfect one. That's the real secret to my success.
{break}
Mix in **fish** with your dirt at my **composter** here and sprinkle the fertilizer on your plants. They'll grow in a jiffy.

That's it! With my secret fertilizer mix, you should be able to grow plants just as well as any farmer in Brickleberry. I'm sure you'll see a significant improvement in your crops.
{break}
Remember, this is our little secret. Don't go telling anyone else about it, or I'll deny everything.
{break}
By the way, if you're looking for some work, you might want to check out the Farming **bounty board** in town. They always have some tasks for skilled farmers like yourself. It's a good way to earn some extra gold and improve your farming skills.

{username}
{break}
As a member of The Collective, it's your time to choose which skill you want to hone to get us a step closer to defeating this thing. Meet me in The Grove and I can help you in your decision.
{break}
— Hoshi

Dude, I've been doing some experimenting on my own with Muck Sucker fish, and I've discovered something amazing. {break} It turns out that these fish can actually change how the mushrooms are purified. {break} The spores that the Muck Suckers produce are incredibly sensitive and can only grow in **caves**, but they're somehow different from the ones we've been working with.
{break}
I can't get the Muck Suckers myself, but if you could supply me with some, I'd be willing to share my method with you. It could be a win-win situation for both of us.
{break}
What do you say, dude? Are you up for the challenge? If so, let me know, bring **18 Muck Suckers** and I'll share the details of my method with you.

Dude, you've really come through for me! These Muck Suckers are exactly what I needed to take my mushroom purification process to the next level.
{break}
I'll only take 10 since you'll need your own Muck Suckers for this, dude! We gotta look out for each other, man.

Here's what I've discovered: if you take the Muck Sucker fish and grind them up into a fine powder, you can use that powder to add to the muckshroom spores in the seed mill. {break}
The resulting purified spores will have a much higher yield than before and will grow into even more robust mushrooms.
{break}
Of course, the process of grinding up the Muck Suckers is a bit messy and time-consuming, but the results are totally worth it. {break}And since you were kind enough to supply me with the fish, I'm willing to share this secret process with you.
{break}
Give it a try and let me know how it works for you. I have a feeling that we're on the brink of something huge here. Remember to plant them **in the dark**

Dude, these purple mushrooms look so rad!
{break}
I've been thinking about that too, actually. I'm curious to see what kind of properties **other types of mushrooms** might have, and how we could use our purification process to unlock their full potential. I mean, who knows what kind of new and exciting flavors we might be able to create with purified mushrooms?
{break}
We should definitely keep experimenting and see what we come up with. Who knows, maybe we'll discover something truly groundbreaking.
{break}
If you're looking to sell those shrooms, you should check out the **bounty board** in town. A lot of other farmers and traders use it to trade and sell different plants and materials, so you might be able to find a buyer there.

{playerName}, I have to say, I'm really impressed with your mining skills. You were able to get that basalt so quickly, and the quality of the bricks you made was exceptional.
{break}
Well, I originally hired you for your skills in working with basalt, but now I'm thinking you might have some talent in mining in general. 
{break}
Would you be interested in taking on another mining project for me?
{break}
I'm actually in need of some silver ore for a project I'm working on. 
{break}
Would you be able to gather some for me? I'll show you how to smelt silver ore into silver bars and cubes, and you can use this technique for all metals.
{break}
You can find **silver ore** as raw ores, deep within **caves.** Your **cleansing flare** may come in handy.

{playerName}, welcome back! Did you manage to gather the silver ore I asked for?
{break}
Excellent work! I have a little something for you. These are molds for metal bars and cubes.
{break}
With this mold, you'll be able to turn that silver ore into silver bars, just like you did with basalt.
{break}
I'll need at least 5 silver bars for my project. Can you handle that?

By the way, those molds can be used for any metal ore, not just silver. So feel free to experiment with them if you come across any other ores.
{break}
Also, I have to say, you have a real knack for mining. You can craft some of this silver for yourself to create new tools with, which can make mining even faster and more efficient.
{break}
If you're interested in more work, you should check out the mining board. There are always people looking for skilled miners like yourself.
